nglish Channel", "emoji": "\u26f5"}], "answer": "irish-sea", "explanation": "The Irish Sea lies between Great Britain and Ireland.", "wrongFeedback": "Look for the sea between the two land areas: it is the Irish Sea."}, "Which waterway is south of England?": {"id": "uk-sea-south", "type": "uk-place", "prompt": "Which waterway is south of England?", "options": [{"id": "english-channel", "label": "English Channel", "emoji": "\u26f5"}, {"id": "irish-sea", "label": "Irish Sea", "emoji": "\ud83d\udc0b"}, {"id": "north-sea", "label": "North Sea", "emoji": "\ud83d\udc1a"}], "answer": "english-channel", "explanation": "The English Channel is south of England.", "wrongFeedback": "The English Channel is the waterway south of England."}, "Which ocean is between the Americas and Europe/Africa?": {"id": "ocean-atlantic", "type": "ocean", "prompt": "Which ocean is between the Americas and Europe/Africa?", "answer": "atlantic", "explanation": "The Atlantic Ocean sits between these continents."}, "Which ocean is between Africa, Asia and Australia?": {"id": "ocean-indian", "type": "ocean", "prompt": "Which ocean is between Africa, Asia and Australia?", "answer": "indian", "explanation": "The Indian Ocean is between Africa, Asia and Australia."}, "Which tool is shaped more like the round Earth?": {"id": "map-globe", "type": "feature", "prompt": "Which tool is shaped more like the round Earth?", "options": [{"id": "globe", "label": "A globe", "emoji": "\ud83c\udf0e"}, {"id": "flat-map", "label": "A flat map", "emoji": "\ud83d\uddfa\ufe0f"}, {"id": "ruler", "label": "A ruler", "emoji": "\ud83d\udccf"}], "answer": "globe", "explanation": "A globe is a round model of Earth. A flat map spreads places onto a page or screen.", "wrongFeedback": "Earth is round, so a globe is the round model. A map is usually flat."}, "Why might an explorer use a flat map?": {"id": "map-flat-purpose", "type": "feature", "prompt": "Why might an explorer use a flat map?", "options": [{"id": "spread-page", "labe