], "answer": "clear-glass", "explanation": "Clear glass is transparent, so we can see through it. The window is the object; glass is its material.", "wrongFeedback": "Think about the property the object needs. A window needs a transparent material."}, "Which season often has the warmest days?": {"id": "science-season", "type": "classify", "prompt": "Which season often has the warmest days?", "options": [{"id": "summer", "label": "Summer", "emoji": "\u2600\ufe0f"}, {"id": "winter", "label": "Winter", "emoji": "\u2744\ufe0f"}, {"id": "autumn", "label": "Autumn", "emoji": "\ud83c\udf42"}], "answer": "summer", "explanation": "Summer often has the warmest days, although weather can change.", "wrongFeedback": "Winter is usually colder. Summer often has the warmest days."}, "Which animal is a mammal?": {"id": "science-animal-mammal", "type": "classify", "prompt": "Which animal is a mammal?", "options": [{"id": "rabbit", "label": "Rabbit", "emoji": "\ud83d\udc07"}, {"id": "trout", "label": "Trout", "emoji": "\ud83d\udc1f"}, {"id": "frog", "label": "Frog", "emoji": "\ud83d\udc38"}], "answer": "rabbit", "explanation": "A rabbit is a mammal. Trout are fish and frogs are amphibians.", "wrongFeedback": "A rabbit is a mammal. Look at the group names: fish, amphibians, reptiles, birds and mammals."}, "Which animal is a bird?": {"id": "science-animal-bird", "type": "classify", "prompt": "Which animal is a bird?", "options": [{"id": "robin", "label": "Robin", "emoji": "\ud83d\udc26"}, {"id": "lizard", "label": "Lizard", "emoji": "\ud83e\udd8e"}, {"id": "cat", "label": "Cat", "emoji": "\ud83d\udc08"}], "answer": "robin", "explanation": "A robin is a bird. A lizard is a reptile and a cat is a mammal.", "wrongFeedback": "A robin is a bird. A lizard is a reptile and a cat is a mammal."}, "What does a green plant need to grow?": {"id": "science-plant-needs", "type": "classify", "prompt": "What does a green plant need to grow?", "options": [{"id": "water-light", "label": "Water and light", "emoji": "\ud83d\udca7"}, {"id": "television", "label": "A television", "emoji": "\ud83d\udcfa"}, {"id": "sandwich", "label": "A sandwich", "emoji": "\ud83e\udd6a"}], "answer": "water-light", "explanation": "Plants need water and light to grow.", "wrongFeedback": "Plants need water and light, not a television or a sandwich."}, "Which part of a plant takes in water from the soil?": {"id": "science-plant-part", "type": "classify", "prompt": "Which part of a plant takes in water from the soil?", "options": [{"id": "roots", "label": "Roots", "emoji": "\ud83c\udf31"}, {"id": "flower", "label": "Flower", "emoji": "\ud83c\udf38"}, {"id": "leaf", "label": "Leaf", "emoji": "\ud83c\udf43"}], "answer": "roots", "explanation": "Roots take in water from the soil and help hold the plant in place.", "wrongFeedback": "Look below the soil: roots take in water and hold the plant."}, "A scientist wants to see how a plant changes. What should they do?": {"id": "science-enquiry", "type": "classify", "prompt": "A scientist wants to see how a plant changes. What should they do?", "options": [{"id": "observe-record", "label": "Observe and record", "emoji": "\ud83d\udd0e"}, {"id": "guess-once", "label": "Guess once", "emoji": "\ud83c\udfb2"}, {"id": "hide-it", "label": "Hide the plant", "emoji": "\ud83d\ude48"}], "answer": "observe-record", "explanation": "Scientists observe closely and record changes over time.", "wrongFeedback": "A fair investigation needs careful observations and records, not one guess."}, "Predict: two similar seedlings get the same light and warmth. Only one gets water. What might happen?": {"id": "science-water-test", "type": "investigation", "prompt": "Predict: two similar seedlings get the same light and warmth. Only one gets water. What might happen?", "predictions": [{"id": "watered-grows", "label": "The watered seedling grows better", "emoji": "\ud83c\udf31"}, {"id": "same-growth", "label": "They grow the same", "emoji": "\ud83e\udd14"}], "observation": "After seven days, the watered seedling is green and taller. The seedling without water has wilted.", "options": [{"id": "water-matters", "label": "Water helped the seedling grow", "emoji": "\ud83d\udca7"}, {"id": "water-never-matters", "label": "Water never matters", "emoji": "\ud83d\udeab"}, {"id": "no-observation", "label": "We learned nothing", "emoji": "\ud83d\ude48"}], "answer": "water-matters", "explanation": "Your prediction came first. Then you compared it with the observation. This test gives evidence that growing seedlings need water.", "wrongFeedback": "Use what was observed: the watered seedling grew better in this test."}, "Which animal is a herbivore?": {"id": "science-animal-food", "type": "classify", "prompt": "Which animal is a herbivore?", "options": [{"id": "cow", "label": "Cow", "emoji": "\ud83d\udc04"}, {"id": "lion", "label": "Lion", "emoji": "\ud83e\udd81"}, {"id": "fox", "label": "Fox", "emoji": "\ud83e\udd8a"}], "answer": "cow", "explanation": "A cow is a herbivore because it eats plants. A lion is a carnivore and a fox can eat both plants and animals.", "wrongFeedback": "Herbivores eat plants. A cow is the herbivore here."}, "Which word describes an animal that eats plants and other animals?": {"id": "science-animal-omnivore", "type": "classify", "prompt": "Which word describes an animal that eats plants and other animals?", "options": [{"id": "omnivore", "label": "Omnivore", "emoji": "\ud83d\udc3b"}, {"id": "herbivore", "label": "Herbivore", "emoji": "\ud83d\udc30"}, {"id": "carnivore", "label": "Carnivore", "emoji": "\ud83e\udd81"}], "answer": "omnivore", "explanation": "An omnivore eats plants and other animals.", "wrongFeedback": "An omnivore eats both plants and other animals."}, "Which body part is linked with seeing?": {"id": "science-sense-eyes", "type": "classify", "prompt": "Which body part is linked with seeing?", "options": [{"id": "eyes", "label": "Eyes", "emoji": "\ud83d\udc40"}, {"id": "ears", "label": "Ears", "emoji": "\ud83d\udc4